within Pharmacolibrary.UsersGuide;

class ReleaseNotes
  extends Modelica.Icons.ReleaseNotes;
  annotation(
    Documentation(info = "<html><head></head><body><h5>Version 26.11</h5><ul><li><b>Machine-generated drug models removed.</b> The models generated in 06/2025 (one per ATC code, parameters written by an LLM with no reviewed source) are gone: 5,684 models and the 5,466 ATC packages they left empty. Kept: models hand-tuned or revised by a person (Allopurinol, Caffeine, Digoxin_1, Digoxin_IV, Fluorouracil, Ibuprofen, Lithium, NitricOxide_1C, Nirsevimab_IM, Propofol) and every hand-written model. <b>This is not converted:</b> a model that extends a removed Drugs class has no replacement; release v26.03 (library version 25.09) is the last one that contains them.</li><li><b>Models extracted from papers</b>, for 377 drugs: 396 PK, 278 PD and 1 PGx model, built by pharmacolibrary-dev from population-PK and PD papers and accepted by its automatic reviewer (the model reproduces the paper's reference values; not checked by a person). {Drug} is the default: an alias of the preferred extracted model (316 drugs).</li><li><b>NonDrugs.T_toxic_hazardous</b>: 188 toxicokinetic and 2 toxicodynamic models for 65 substances of the toxin knowledge base, most of them retention functions (Pharmacokinetic.Models.TK_Retention).</li><li>A drug whose ATC code had no package gets one ({code}_{Drug}); the ATC tree holds only packages with a model: 123 level-3 and 453 level-5 packages.</li><li><b>Resources/Models/index.csv</b> lists every extracted model: class, kind, template, source paper (DOI, PMID), review status and its page on the documentation site.</li><li>Examples: Paracetamol_Experiment uses Paracetamol_Langeskov2022_reference with an explicit dose (3 x 1000 mg); ExplanationComponents and ExplanationComponents2 declare their parameters.</li><li>Tested in OpenModelica 1.26.3: every model of Examples, Drugs and NonDrugs passes the check, and the extracted PK models reproduce the reference peaks of the pipeline's simulation.</li><li><b>Drugs.ATC and Drugs.Common removed.</b> Each generated model Drugs.ATC.{L1}.{code} was folded into its model in the ATC packages (Drugs.{L1}_….{L3}_….{code}_{Drug}.{Drug}), which now extends the Pharmacokinetic template directly; models that modified the ATC model keep their own values.</li><li>A model extending Drugs.ATC.… is converted on load (Resources/Scripts/Conversion/ConvertFromPharmacolibrary_25.09.mos) when its drug still has a model. Drugs.Common.DrugData (molecular data) has no replacement: models set the molar mass as a parameter.</li><li>Examples that extended Drugs.ATC models extend the template with the same values.</li><li><b>Drugs.Substances</b>: one package of constants per drug (4,013): name, own ATC codes, DrugBank / PubChem / ChEBI / Wikidata ids, formula, molar mass (PubChem), logP and the metabolites of its extracted models (e.g. Substances.Clopidogrel.ClopidogrelH4.M), with a short summary of the drug. Interfaces.PartialSubstance / PartialMetabolite define the constants.</li><li>Paracetamol_healthy: molar mass is a parameter (it read a field the record did not have).</li><li><b>DevModels not in the release.</b> The work-in-progress package <code>DevModels</code> (40 of its 67 models do not pass checkModel) stays on the <code>main</code> branch of the repository and is left out of released versions. Not converted. The 24 editor backup files (<code>.bak-mo</code>) in Examples are removed.</li></ul><h5><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: -webkit-standard; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: auto; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: auto; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4); -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;\"></ul></h5><h5 style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: -webkit-standard; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: auto; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: auto; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4); -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;\">Version 25.08-beta1</h5><div><ul><li>generated models of all drugs in Drugs.ATC</li><li>tested in OpenModelica 1.25 and Dymola 2025</li><li>added example of PKPD integrated with Physiolibrary 3.0.0</li><li>added example of PGx with various combination of pharmacogene mutation and it's influence on PK</li></ul></div><h5>Version 25.05-beta.3</h5>
<ul>
<li>Introduction of first version&nbsp;</li></ul>

</body></html>"));
end ReleaseNotes;